WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.440
If your prep is PEG, this video will walk you through exactly how to take it.

2
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:06.320
Just follow along step by step.

3
00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:09.340
Your PEG prep is the large container that you'll mix with water.

4
00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:13.320
You'll also want Crystal Light or flavor packs on hand if you'd like to improve

5
00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:13.920
the taste.

6
00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:17.160
At 8 a.m. the day before your procedure, you'll mix the prep.

7
00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:21.140
Add water to your prep container and stir or shake until everything is fully

8
00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:21.960
dissolved.

9
00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:24.400
Once it's mixed, put it in the refrigerator.

10
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:27.100
Keeping it cold makes it much easier to drink.

11
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:30.460
If you're adding Crystal Light or a flavor pack, you can mix that in now.

12
00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:33.360
Just make sure it's not red, orange, blue, or purple.

13
00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:36.380
Stick to clear or light-colored flavors.

14
00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:39.460
Between 4 and 5 p.m., you'll begin drinking the solution.

15
00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:40.700
Here's the pace.

16
00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:44.800
Drink 16 ounces, that's about two cups, every 30 minutes.

17
00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:48.490
You'll keep going at that pace for about 4 hours until the entire container

18
00:00:48.490 --> 00:00:49.220
is empty.

19
00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:50.660
Take your time with each glass.

20
00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:54.650
Slow, steady sips are easier on your stomach than trying to gulp it all at once

21
00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:54.940
.

22
00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:56.900
This part is really important.

23
00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:01.490
You must drink all of the prep solution as directed, even if you're already

24
00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:03.500
passing clear liquid.

25
00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:07.490
I know it can feel like enough, but finishing the entire dose is what gives us

26
00:01:07.490 --> 00:01:10.020
the clearest view during your procedure.

27
00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:14.260
If the prep isn't completed as directed, we may need to reschedule, and neither

28
00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:15.260
of us wants that.

29
00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:18.980
Once you've finished, keep drinking clear liquids until bedtime.

30
00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:22.820
Staying hydrated will help you feel better and help the prep do its job.

31
00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:27.200
If you experience any discomfort from frequent trips to the bathroom, applying

32
00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:30.980
a petroleum-based ointment or diaper rash cream can really help.

33
00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:33.540
That's it, you've got this.

34
00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:37.620
Follow the timing, finish the full dose, and stay hydrated.

35
00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:40.990
If you have any questions at all, don't hesitate to call our office, we're here

36
00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:41.540
to help.
